   "input": "/bin/zsh -c 'cat /var/folders/3g/vf36b0b14wzd0fgsgtdp06h00000gp/T/writing-probe/p-3d9e16d4/471ff4ef.txt'",
   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# See inside a ZIP archive with sackview\n\nCheck archive entries and sizes before you unpack them.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nZIP archives only \u00b7 Offline inspection \u00b7 No archive changes\n\n## Inspect an archive\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\n### List entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\n### Find the largest entries\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\n### Filter by name\n\nShow only entries whose names match the pattern:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\n## Keys\n\nKeyboard shortcuts are not specified.\n\n## Check disk space before extracting\n\nsackview displays the total unpacked size. Use this total to check available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\n## Good to know\n\n- **Archive contents:** sackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n- **Privacy:** inspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n- **Supported formats:** sackview supports ZIP archives only. Other formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code `24`.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What does sackview show you?\n(b) What command lists the entries in photos.zip?\n(c) Does sackview extract files?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (c) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
